# Resolution: Release pipeline dry-run test

## Validation Checklist
- [x] All gauntlet steps green (fmt, clippy -D warnings, 22 Rust suites, wasm build, 70 JS tests, zero-dep tree)
- [x] Secret scans zero hits (tree + full history)
- [x] Registry dry-runs validated (pnpm pack x5, cargo publish --dry-run eval, package --list rest)
- [x] PR CI fully green: 7/7 checks on all 3 OSes

## Outcomes / Summary
The dry-run test caught and fixed four real pipeline defects:
1. GitHub workflows never ran scripts/ci-stub-rust-cuda-crates.sh -> all cargo jobs failed on
   the missing /projects/github/rust-cuda absolute-path deps. Now wired into all 5 jobs with
   sudo on Linux, drive-prefix STUB_ROOT on Windows, and driver workspace-exclusion on macOS
   (sealed root FS).
2. Stub lib.rs files were zero-byte and failed cargo fmt --all --check (fmt formats path deps).
3. release-crates dry-run used cargo package --no-verify, which cannot resolve pre-first-publish
   internal deps -> switched to cargo package --list until the chain is on crates.io.
4. npm audit blocked on the vulnerable protobufjs/grpc chain from firebase 9 (auto-installed
   peer): store peers widened to firebase 9-12 / better-sqlite3 8-12, firebase ^12 pinned as
   devDep, audit gate now --prod and genuinely clean.
Also documented: gh workflow run cannot dispatch release workflows until they exist on main.
